/* zh-SG translations for "think" (generated by tools/i18n-pack.js; keys are the English source). */
Object.assign(window.I18N['zh-SG'].text, {
  "Why does spending feel like love?": "为什么花钱会感觉像爱？",
  "A gift, a treat, a \"top gifter\" badge. Why does paying for someone feel like caring for them?": "一份礼物、一顿请客、一个“榜一大哥”徽章。为什么替一个人付钱，会感觉像是在关心对方？",
  "Ads, feeds and checkout buttons are designed by very smart people to link spending with feelings: belonging, status, being a good partner. Instalments and \"buy now, pay later\" make the price feel smaller than it is.": "广告、动态和结账按钮，都是由非常聪明的人设计的，目的是把花钱和感受连在一起：归属感、身份地位、做一个好伴侣。分期付款和“先买后付”会让价格感觉比实际更小。",
  "You still choose. A budget you set calmly beats a decision made at 1 a.m. with a heart emoji on screen. The most remembered gifts are usually time, attention and something handmade.": "你依然可以选择。冷静时订下的预算，胜过凌晨1点、屏幕上带着爱心表情时做的决定。最让人记得的礼物，通常是时间、用心，以及亲手做的东西。",
  "Families differ. For some, generous gifts and treating others show respect and \"face\"; for others, saving is the respectful thing. Neither is wrong, but it helps to know which one you grew up with.": "每个家庭都不一样。对有些家庭来说，大方送礼和请客代表尊重和“面子”；对另一些家庭来说，节省才是尊重。两者都没错，但知道自己是在哪一种家庭长大的，会很有帮助。",
  "MoneySense says credit card interest here is about 25% to 29% a year on any unpaid balance. Paying only the minimum on a $5,000 bill can take about 14.5 years.": "根据MoneySense，这里的信用卡对未还清余额收取的年利率大约是25%到29%。一张$5,000的账单如果只付最低还款，可能要花大约14.5年才能还清。",
  "MoneySense, the national financial literacy programme, advises paying off the highest-interest debt first, including instalment plans.": "全国理财教育计划MoneySense建议，先还清利率最高的债务，包括分期付款计划。",
  "The pull to spend is built into the system around you. That is not your partner's fault, and it is not a test of love.": "想花钱的冲动，是你周围的整个系统设计出来的。那不是你另一半的错，也不是爱的考验。",
  "Which of these explains your last impulse buy best?": "下面哪一个最能解释你上一次的冲动消费？",
  "Online it's \"men vs women\". Is it?": "网上都在说“男人 vs 女人”。真的是这样吗？",
  "Your feed says boys and girls are enemies: one side has it easy, the other side pays. Who gains from that story?": "你的动态说男生和女生是敌人：一方占尽便宜，另一方买单。谁会从这个说法中得益？",
  "Costs and platforms": "成本与平台",
  "Rising costs of housing, weddings and raising children squeeze young men and young women at the same time. Outrage also earns clicks: platforms tend to reward posts that make groups angry at each other, because anger keeps people scrolling.": "房价、婚礼和养育孩子的成本不断上升，同时挤压着年轻男性和年轻女性。愤怒也能换来点击率：平台往往会奖励那些让群体互相仇视的帖子，因为愤怒会让人一直滑下去。",
  "Whatever the feed says, each couple can set its own fair terms: who pays for what, who does which chores, whose career goes first and when. Real people are not averages.": "不管动态怎么说，每一对情侣都可以订下自己的公平规则：谁付什么、谁做哪些家务、谁的事业先、什么时候。真实的人不是平均数。",
  "Many parents grew up with \"the man provides, the woman cares\". Some couples still like that; many want something else. Expectations from home shape what each of you thinks is \"fair\" before you even talk.": "很多父母是在“男主外、女主内”的观念下长大的。有些情侣现在仍然喜欢这样；很多人想要的是别的模式。在你们开口谈之前，家里的期望就已经塑造了你们各自心中的“公平”。",
  "Male citizens and second-generation permanent residents serve about two years of full-time National Service, usually right after school.": "男性公民和第二代永久居民通常在毕业后就要服大约两年的全职国民服役。",
  "The Ministry of Manpower reported a 14.3% pay gap between men and women in 2023, or 6.0% when comparing similar jobs and hours. It names job types, caregiving and discrimination as causes.": "人力部报告指出，2023年男女薪资差距为14.3%，比较相似的工作和工时则为6.0%。报告列出的原因包括职业类型、照顾家人的责任和歧视。",
  "Both of you are facing the same price tags. A war between the two of you is the least useful fight available.": "你们两个面对的是同样的价格标签。你们两个之间的战争，是最没用的一场仗。",
  "Which lens feels closest to what you see around you?": "哪一个视角最接近你在身边看到的情况？",
  "Whose expectations are these?": "这些是谁的期望？",
  "Grades, the \"right\" course, the \"right\" job. When you imagine failing, whose face do you see?": "成绩、“对的”科系、“对的”工作。当你想象自己失败时，你看到的是谁的脸？",
  "A small, competitive economy rewards credentials, and entry to courses and scholarships is decided by results. The pressure is real, and it was not invented by your parents or your partner.": "一个小而竞争激烈的经济体奖励学历，而科系和奖学金的录取是由成绩决定的。压力是真实的，而且不是你父母或另一半发明出来的。",
  "Effort matters, and so does rest. You also get to write your own definition of success: a job you can grow in, a life with time for people and the things you love.": "努力很重要，休息也一样。你也可以写下自己对成功的定义：一份能让你成长的工作、一个有时间留给人和你热爱之事的生活。",
  "Many parents sacrificed a lot so their children could study. Their hopes often come from love and fear at the same time. You can honour that and still choose your path, with a plan.": "很多父母牺牲了很多，好让孩子能读书。他们的期望往往同时来自爱和恐惧。你可以尊重这一点，同时带着计划选择自己的路。",
  "Many scholarships come with a bond. PSC undergraduate scholarships, for example, usually mean four to six years of work for the government after graduating.": "很多奖学金都附带服务合约。比如公共服务委员会（PSC）的本科奖学金，通常意味着毕业后要为政府工作四到六年。",
  "Every Singaporean aged 25 and above receives SkillsFuture Credit for courses, with more for mid-career workers aged 40 and above. Learning does not end at your A-levels.": "每一位25岁及以上的新加坡人都会获得用于上课的技能创前程（SkillsFuture）补助金，40岁及以上的中年员工还会获得更多。学习不会在A水准考完后就结束。",
  "Exam stress is a weather system over everyone in the cohort. Help each other through it instead of making it a contest.": "考试压力就像笼罩着整个年级的天气系统。互相帮忙撑过去，而不是把它变成一场比赛。",
  "Where does most of your pressure come from right now?": "你现在大部分的压力来自哪里？",
  "Two years \"behind\"?": "“落后”了两年？",
  "Haziq says: \"By the time we ORD, the girls in our batch are already in year two of uni.\" Is anyone actually behind?": "哈齐克说：“等我们退役（ORD）的时候，我们那一届的女生都已经读到大学二年级了。”真的有人落后了吗？",
  "National needs set the NS timeline. Different people lose different years to different things: service, caregiving, illness, a parent's job abroad. Timelines were never equal to begin with.": "国家的需要决定了国民服役的时间表。不同的人因为不同的事情失去不同的年份：服役、照顾家人、生病、父母被派驻国外。时间表本来就从来不是平等的。",
  "What matters is how you use the time: skills, fitness, friendships, savings, a clearer idea of what you want to study. Two years can be a head start in maturity.": "重要的是你怎么运用这段时间：技能、体能、友情、储蓄，还有对自己想读什么更清楚的想法。两年，可以是成熟度上的领先。",
  "For many families, NS is a point of pride, and also a time of worry. Your parents may have their own stories about it. Ask them.": "对很多家庭来说，国民服役是一件值得骄傲的事，也是一段让人担心的时期。你的父母可能有他们自己关于国民服役的故事。去问问他们。",
  "Full-time National Service lasts two years for most servicemen, followed by years of reservist training.": "大部分军人的全职国民服役为期两年，之后还有好几年的战备军人训练。",
  "MOM notes that women here still shoulder more of the care for children and elders, which also shapes career timelines.": "人力部指出，这里的女性依然承担了更多照顾孩子和长辈的责任，这也影响了她们的职业时间表。",
  "Comparing timelines turns partners into rivals. You are not racing each other; you are both on a road with different bumps.": "比较时间表会把伴侣变成对手。你们不是在跟对方赛跑；你们都在路上，只是遇到的坑不一样。",
  "Which lens would you share with Haziq?": "你会跟哈齐克分享哪一个视角？",
  "Who looks after Ah Ma?": "谁来照顾阿嬷？",
  "Mum on the phone: \"Your grandmother fell again.\" Who is going to care for her, and who pays?": "妈妈在电话里说：“你外婆又跌倒了。”谁来照顾她？谁来付钱？",
  "A lot of care for elders is unpaid work done at home, and it often falls on daughters and daughters-in-law, sometimes while they also raise children: the \"sandwich generation\".": "很多照顾长辈的工作都是在家里进行的无偿劳动，而且往往落在女儿和媳妇身上，有时她们同时还在养育孩子：也就是“三明治一代”。",
  "Planning helps: talk early with siblings and your partner, save a little, learn what support exists, and show up regularly, even in small ways like a weekly visit.": "计划会有帮助：早点跟兄弟姐妹和另一半谈，存一点钱，了解有哪些支援，并且定期出现，哪怕只是像每星期探望一次这样的小事。",
  "Filial piety and multigenerational homes are important to many families here. Others prefer independent living with support nearby. Couples often come from both kinds of family.": "孝道和几代同堂的家庭，对这里的很多家庭来说都很重要。也有人比较喜欢独立生活，同时在附近有支援。很多情侣就分别来自这两种家庭。",
  "You can top up a parent's or grandparent's CPF retirement account. Eligible seniors with lower savings get a matching government grant of up to $2,000 a year.": "你可以为父母或祖父母的公积金（CPF）退休户头填补款项。储蓄较少的合格乐龄人士，每年可以获得最高$2,000的政府对等补助。",
  "The Agency for Integrated Care lists caregiver support, respite care and grants such as the Home Caregiving Grant.": "护联中心（Agency for Integrated Care）列出了照顾者支援、暂托服务，以及居家护理补助金等津贴。",
  "Ageing parents are a family project, not a test of which partner loves their side more.": "父母年老是一个家庭项目，不是用来考验哪一方更爱自己家人的测试。",
  "What did your family teach you about caring for elders?": "关于照顾长辈，你的家庭教了你什么？",
  "Who pays for a child?": "养一个孩子，谁来付？",
  "Mei, holding her colleague's newborn at a full-month party: \"Everyone asks when they're having the second one. Nobody asks who's going to sleep.\"": "小美在同事宝宝的满月宴上，抱着那个新生儿说：“大家都在问他们什么时候生第二个。没有人问谁来熬夜。”",
  "Much of the cost of raising children is unpaid time: night feeds, sick days, school runs. When budgets and leave are tight, it turns into \"who sacrifices?\" fights between partners.": "养育孩子的很多成本都是无偿的时间：半夜喂奶、孩子生病的日子、接送上下学。当预算和假期都很紧的时候，就会变成伴侣之间“谁来牺牲？”的争吵。",
  "Readiness is a shared choice: money, health, where you will live, who takes leave, and whether you both want it at all. Talking about it early is part of loving someone.": "准备好了没有，是一个共同的选择：钱、健康、住在哪里、谁请假，以及你们两个到底想不想要。早点谈这件事，就是爱一个人的一部分。",
  "Relatives may ask \"when got baby?\" at every reunion dinner. Their excitement is often love, but the decision belongs to the couple.": "亲戚可能在每一次团圆饭上都问“几时生孩子？”他们的兴奋往往是出于爱，但决定权在这对夫妻手上。",
  "The Baby Bonus Scheme gives $11,000 in cash for a first child plus a Child Development Account with government co-matching. A new SG Child Support Package announced in 2026 will replace it.": "婴儿花红计划为第一胎提供$11,000现金，外加一个由政府共同配对的儿童培育户头。2026年宣布的新版新加坡儿童援助配套将取代它。",
  "From 1 April 2026, parents get up to 30 weeks of paid leave in total: 16 weeks maternity, 4 weeks paternity and 10 weeks shared between both parents.": "从2026年4月1日起，父母总共可以获得最多30个星期的带薪假期：16个星期产假、4个星期陪产假，以及10个星期由父母双方共享的育儿假。",
  "Sleepless nights and childcare fees are a shared problem to solve, not a score to keep against each other.": "不眠之夜和托儿费是一个需要一起解决的问题，而不是用来互相记分的。",
  "If you have children one day, what would \"fair\" look like to you?": "如果你以后有孩子，对你来说“公平”是什么样子？",
  "Us vs the problem": "我们 vs. 问题",
  "BTO queue, wedding banquet, renovation, a family who wants a big celebration. It is easy to start blaming each other.": "预购组屋的排队、婚宴、装修，还有一个想要大肆庆祝的家庭。很容易就开始互相指责。",
  "Fights between men and women often hide a pressure from above: housing prices, care work and wages. Societies share these costs differently between the state, employers and families, and every model strains when growth slows.": "男女之间的争吵，往往掩盖了来自上层的压力：房价、照顾工作和工资。不同的社会以不同的方式在国家、雇主和家庭之间分担这些成本，而当经济增长放缓时，每一种模式都会承受压力。",
  "A budget you both choose beats a budget your relatives choose. Decide what matters most to you two, write down the numbers, and leave room for savings.": "你们两个一起选择的预算，胜过亲戚替你们选择的预算。决定对你们两个来说什么最重要，把数字写下来，并且留一些储蓄的空间。",
  "Wedding customs differ: banquets, hantaran, dowry traditions, church weddings, simple ROM ceremonies. Many couples blend customs from two families. Talk about it before the aunties do.": "婚礼习俗各不相同：婚宴、马来族的聘礼（hantaran）、嫁妆传统、教堂婚礼、简单的婚姻注册局（ROM）仪式。很多情侣会融合两个家庭的习俗。在阿姨们开口之前，你们先谈。",
  "First-timer couples can get an Enhanced CPF Housing Grant of up to $120,000, depending on household income.": "首次购屋的夫妻，可以根据家庭收入获得最高$120,000的加强版公积金购屋津贴。",
  "BTO flats are built after launch, so many couples wait years for keys. Some 2026 launches are Shorter Waiting Time flats with waits under three years.": "预购组屋是推出后才开始建造的，所以很多夫妻要等好几年才能拿到钥匙。2026年的一些推出项目属于短等候期组屋，等候时间少于三年。",
  "Put the problem on the table between you, not between you and her. Then solve it as a team.": "把问题放在你们两个之间的桌子上，而不是放在你和她之间。然后像一个团队一样去解决它。",
  "Which lens helps you two most right now?": "哪一个视角现在对你们两个最有帮助？"
});
